From: waydroid-nvidia-prolapse
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: Tell Mesa NVK apart from the NVIDIA proprietary driver

Base: https://chromium.googlesource.com/angle/angle c1a25085dd9e4a8cd6c72be278c0b4bdf6ce2824
plus 0001. Apply with `git apply` after 0001. Current main (7865acacb) has the
same code: no VkDriverId check for NVIDIA.

NVK (Mesa's Vulkan driver for NVIDIA GPUs) reports NVIDIA's vendor ID, so
Renderer::initFeatures() treated it as the NVIDIA proprietary driver. It
parsed NVK's Mesa-style driverVersion (VK_MAKE_VERSION(26, 2, 5)) with the
NVIDIA layout, which reads as driver "26.x", and then applied every
workaround meant for NVIDIA drivers older than 421/441/470/525/531.

The one that hurts most is externallySynchronizePipelineCacheAccess (NVIDIA
< 441): every vkCreateGraphicsPipelines of the link-time warm-up tasks runs
under one renderer mutex, so ANGLE's worker pool compiles one pipeline at a
time and the draw that waits for the warm-up stalls. NVK's VkPipelineCache
is internally synchronized (Mesa src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline_cache.c,
simple_mtx around the object cache), as the Vulkan spec requires unless
VK_PIPELINE_CACHE_CREATE_EXTERNALLY_SYNCHRONIZED_BIT is set.

Measured on an RTX 5090 with NVK (Mesa 26.2.5) under Android 13, Minecraft
Bedrock 1.26.60.24, first hotbar switch (longest present-to-present
interval of the app's layer):
  before: 1542 ms; the render thread is idle while one worker at a time
          runs NVK's compiler
  with externallySynchronizePipelineCacheAccess disabled alone: 186 ms,
          all 16 worker threads compile concurrently

Following the PanVK split (ba5db43c1, isARMProprietary = isARM &&
!isMesaPanVK), NVK is identified by VkDriverId alone
(VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_NVK) and isNvidiaProprietary = isNvidia && !isMesaNVK:

- driverVersion: parsed as Mesa for NVK (NVIDIA layout only for the
  proprietary driver); getVersionString() likewise.
- isNvidiaProprietary (driver bugs, NVIDIA driver version checks):
  clampPointSize, avoidOpSelectWithMismatchingRelaxedPrecision,
  disableDepthStencilResolveThroughAttachment, avoidInvisibleWindowSwapchainRecreate,
  swapchainDeferredMemoryAllocation, supportsSPIRV14, supportsGraphicsPipelineLibrary,
  externallySynchronizePipelineCacheAccess,
  forceWaitForSubmissionToCompleteForQueryResult, supportsDynamicRenderingLocalRead.
- isNvidia kept (the GPU, not the driver, or a reason that holds for NVK too):
  isImmediateModeRenderer, clampFragDepth (only without
  VK_EXT_depth_clamp_zero_one, which NVK exposes), allowGenerateMipmapWithCompute,
  doubleDepthBiasConstantFactor (unchanged for NVK; the list already holds the
  Mesa drivers of other vendors), preferGlobalPipelineCache,
  skipPipelineCacheSerialization (NVK keeps compiled shaders in its own disk
  cache; a second copy in the blob cache would only duplicate it).
---
diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
index 723c332528..e81caa15dd 100644
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
@@ -215,6 +215,13 @@ bool IsMesaPanVK(uint32_t driverId)
     return driverId == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_PANVK;
 }
 
+bool IsMesaNVK(uint32_t driverId)
+{
+    // NVK reports NVIDIA's vendor ID; rely on VkDriverId alone to tell it apart from the NVIDIA
+    // proprietary driver
+    return driverId == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_NVK;
+}
+
 bool IsQualcommOpenSource(uint32_t vendorId, uint32_t driverId, const char *deviceName)
 {
     if (!IsQualcomm(vendorId))
@@ -5128,7 +5135,8 @@ std::string Renderer::getVersionString(bool includeFullVersion) const
     {
         strstr << "-";
 
-        if (mPhysicalDeviceProperties.vendorID == VENDOR_ID_NVIDIA)
+        if (mPhysicalDeviceProperties.vendorID == VENDOR_ID_NVIDIA &&
+            !IsMesaNVK(mDriverProperties.driverID))
         {
             strstr << ANGLE_VK_VERSION_MAJOR_NVIDIA(driverVersion) << ".";
             strstr << ANGLE_VK_VERSION_MINOR_NVIDIA(driverVersion) << ".";
@@ -5510,6 +5518,12 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     const bool isMesaPanVK      = IsMesaPanVK(mDriverProperties.driverID);
     const bool isARMProprietary = isARM && !isMesaPanVK;
 
+    // Distinguish between the NVIDIA proprietary driver and the Mesa open source driver.  isNvidia
+    // remains true for both and is used where the hardware is what matters; workarounds for
+    // proprietary driver bugs and driver version checks use isNvidiaProprietary.
+    const bool isMesaNVK           = IsMesaNVK(mDriverProperties.driverID);
+    const bool isNvidiaProprietary = isNvidia && !isMesaNVK;
+
     // Lacking other explicit ways to tell if mali GPU is job manager based or command stream front
     // end based, we use maxDrawIndirectCount as equivalent since all JM based has
     // maxDrawIndirectCount==1 and all CSF based has maxDrawIndirectCount>1.
@@ -5530,12 +5544,12 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
         driverVersion =
             angle::ParseQualcommVulkanDriverVersion(mPhysicalDeviceProperties.driverVersion);
     }
-    else if (isNvidia)
+    else if (isNvidiaProprietary)
     {
         driverVersion =
             angle::ParseNvidiaVulkanDriverVersion(mPhysicalDeviceProperties.driverVersion);
     }
-    else if (IsLinux() && (isIntel || isRADV))
+    else if (isMesaNVK || (IsLinux() && (isIntel || isRADV)))
     {
         driverVersion =
             angle::ParseMesaVulkanDriverVersion(mPhysicalDeviceProperties.driverVersion);
@@ -5640,12 +5654,13 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     //   < 421 otherwise
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
         &mFeatures, clampPointSize,
-        isNvidia && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(IsWindows() ? 430 : 421, 0, 0));
+        isNvidiaProprietary && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(IsWindows() ? 430 : 421, 0, 0));
 
     // Affecting Nvidia drivers 535 through 551.
-    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, avoidOpSelectWithMismatchingRelaxedPrecision,
-                            isNvidia && (driverVersion >= angle::VersionTriple(535, 0, 0) &&
-                                         driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(552, 0, 0)));
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
+        &mFeatures, avoidOpSelectWithMismatchingRelaxedPrecision,
+        isNvidiaProprietary && (driverVersion >= angle::VersionTriple(535, 0, 0) &&
+                                driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(552, 0, 0)));
 
     // Affecting Linux/Intel (unknown range).
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, wrapSwitchInIfTrue, isIntel && IsLinux());
@@ -5821,7 +5836,7 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     // - Pixel4: http://anglebug.com/42267096
     //
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, disableDepthStencilResolveThroughAttachment,
-                            isNvidia || isQualcommProprietary);
+                            isNvidiaProprietary || isQualcommProprietary);
 
     // MSRTSS is disabled if the driver does not support it for RGBA8 and RGBA8_SRGB.
     // This is used to filter out known drivers where support for sRGB formats are missing.
@@ -5892,8 +5907,9 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     // - Enable for NVIDIA on Linux X11 because of the possible driver bug, when acquire next image
     //   continuously returns OUT_OF_DATE if recreate the swapchain while window is not visible
     //   (http://anglebug.com/397848903).
-    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, avoidInvisibleWindowSwapchainRecreate,
-                            (isNvidia && nativeWindowSystem == angle::NativeWindowSystem::X11));
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
+        &mFeatures, avoidInvisibleWindowSwapchainRecreate,
+        (isNvidiaProprietary && nativeWindowSystem == angle::NativeWindowSystem::X11));
 
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, padBuffersToMaxVertexAttribStride, isAMD || isSamsung);
     mMaxVertexAttribStride =
@@ -6153,7 +6169,7 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     // http://anglebug.com/499347835
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
         &mFeatures, swapchainDeferredMemoryAllocation,
-        mFeatures.supportsSwapchainMaintenance1.enabled && !(IsWayland() && isNvidia));
+        mFeatures.supportsSwapchainMaintenance1.enabled && !(IsWayland() && isNvidiaProprietary));
 
     // The VK_EXT_legacy_dithering extension enables dithering support without emulation
     // Disable the usage of VK_EXT_legacy_dithering on ARM until the driver bug
@@ -6270,7 +6286,7 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
         &mFeatures, supportsSPIRV14,
         ExtensionFound(VK_KHR_SPIRV_1_4_EXTENSION_NAME, deviceExtensionNames) &&
-            !(isNvidia && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(525, 0, 0)) &&
+            !(isNvidiaProprietary && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(525, 0, 0)) &&
             !(isQualcommProprietary && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(512, 829, 0)) &&
             !(isARMProprietary && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(47, 0, 0)));
 
@@ -6486,10 +6502,11 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     // problematic area gets addressed and fixed. http://anglebug.com/404581992
     //
     // PowerVR graphics pipeline support is in development and not yet tested with ANGLE.
-    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, supportsGraphicsPipelineLibrary,
-                            mGraphicsPipelineLibraryFeatures.graphicsPipelineLibrary == VK_TRUE &&
-                                (!isNvidia || driverVersion >= angle::VersionTriple(531, 0, 0)) &&
-                                !isRADV && !isARMProprietary && !isPowerVR);
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
+        &mFeatures, supportsGraphicsPipelineLibrary,
+        mGraphicsPipelineLibraryFeatures.graphicsPipelineLibrary == VK_TRUE &&
+            (!isNvidiaProprietary || driverVersion >= angle::VersionTriple(531, 0, 0)) && !isRADV &&
+            !isARMProprietary && !isPowerVR);
 
     // When VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library is not used:
     //
@@ -6526,6 +6543,8 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     // For Windows NVIDIA Vulkan driver, Vulkan pipeline cache will only generate one
     // single huge cache for one process shared by all graphics pipelines in the same process,
     // which can be huge. zlib take long time to compress it.
+    // Mesa's NVK keeps compiled shaders in its own on-disk cache, which a copy in the blob cache
+    // would only duplicate.
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, skipPipelineCacheSerialization, isSwiftShader || isNvidia);
 
     // Practically all drivers still prefer to do cross-stage linking.
@@ -6572,10 +6591,11 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     // - mergeProgramPipelineCachesToGlobalCache is enabled
     // - preferMonolithicPipelinesOverLibraries is enabled
     // - stale nvidia drivers
-    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, externallySynchronizePipelineCacheAccess,
-                            mFeatures.mergeProgramPipelineCachesToGlobalCache.enabled ||
-                                mFeatures.preferMonolithicPipelinesOverLibraries.enabled ||
-                                (isNvidia && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(441, 0, 0)));
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
+        &mFeatures, externallySynchronizePipelineCacheAccess,
+        mFeatures.mergeProgramPipelineCachesToGlobalCache.enabled ||
+            mFeatures.preferMonolithicPipelinesOverLibraries.enabled ||
+            (isNvidiaProprietary && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(441, 0, 0)));
 
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, enableAsyncPipelineCacheCompression, true);
 
@@ -6705,9 +6725,9 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     // Workaround for nvidia earlier version driver which appears having a bug that On older nvidia
     // driver, vkGetQueryPoolResult() with VK_QUERY_RESULT_WAIT_BIT may result in incorrect result.
     // In that case we force into CPU wait for submission to complete. http://anglebug.com/42265186
-    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
-        &mFeatures, forceWaitForSubmissionToCompleteForQueryResult,
-        isARMProprietary || (isNvidia && driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(470, 0, 0)));
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, forceWaitForSubmissionToCompleteForQueryResult,
+                            isARMProprietary || (isNvidiaProprietary &&
+                                                 driverVersion < angle::VersionTriple(470, 0, 0)));
 
     // Some ARM proprietary drivers may not free memory in "vkFreeCommandBuffers()" without
     // VK_COMMAND_POOL_CREATE_RESET_COMMAND_BUFFER_BIT flag.
@@ -6777,7 +6797,7 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
         &mFeatures, supportsDynamicRenderingLocalRead,
         mFeatures.supportsDynamicRendering.enabled &&
             mDynamicRenderingLocalReadFeatures.dynamicRenderingLocalRead == VK_TRUE &&
-            !(isNvidia || isSamsung));
+            !(isNvidiaProprietary || isSamsung));
 
     // Using dynamic rendering when VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering_local_read is available, because that's
     // needed for framebuffer fetch, MSRTT and advanced blend emulation.
